--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this mod does with your data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hiding addresses and names changes only what is drawn on screen. The
address Minecraft connects to and the name it stores are never modified.

config/ipaddresshider.json holds the servers whose address or name you
have chosen to hide, and your Streamer Mode setting. It stays on your
computer.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Twitch (optional, off until you connect)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unless you press "Connect Twitch account", this mod makes no network
requests at all.

If you connect, it contacts Twitch (id.twitch.tv and api.twitch.tv) to:

  - sign you in with a short code you confirm on twitch.tv/activate,
  - ask about once a minute whether your channel is live.

It requests no permissions: no chat, no channel management, no e-mail.
The login is stored in config/ipaddresshider-twitch.json, separately from
the normal config so the normal one stays safe to share. "Disconnect
Twitch" revokes the login at Twitch and deletes that file.

After disconnecting, the app may still be listed under Twitch Settings >
Connections. The login it held is already invalid at that point. To
remove the entry as well, click "Disconnect" there.

